" :SongwriterTabChord (songwriter#tab#TabChord, spec [Tablature][[Annotations]]
" 6): write a chord above the tab, aligned to the cursor column, on its
" annotation line, the tab widened to make room when its neighbours are too
" close, else on a new one.

Given (insert chord above tab block at cursor column):
  e|-----------4--|--1-----------|
  B|--------1-----|-----2-----2--|
  G|--3-----0--0--|-----1--0--0--|
  D|--------1-----|-----1--------|
  A|--4--3--------|--1-----1-----|
  E|--3-----------|--1-----------|

Execute (insert chord above tab block at cursor column):
  call cursor(1, 14)
  call songwriter#tab#TabChord('Am7')
Then:
  AssertEqual '             Am7', getline(1)
  AssertEqual 'e|-----------4--|--1-----------|', getline(2)
  AssertEqual 'B|--------1-----|-----2-----2--|', getline(3)

Given (insert chord at column 1 (start of tab)):
  e|--4--|--1--|
  B|------|-----|
  G|------|-----|
  D|------|-----|
  A|------|-----|
  E|------|-----|

Execute (on the string name, the chord goes to the first column that keeps it an annotation):
  call cursor(1, 1)
  call songwriter#tab#TabChord('C')
Then:
  AssertEqual '  C', getline(1)
  AssertEqual 'e|--4--|--1--|', getline(2)

Given (insert chord in middle of tab block):
  e|--4--|--1--|
  B|------|-----|
  G|------|-----|
  D|------|-----|
  A|------|-----|
  E|------|-----|

Execute (insert chord in middle of tab block):
  call cursor(3, 8)
  call songwriter#tab#TabChord('Dm')
Then:
  AssertEqual '       Dm', getline(1)
  AssertEqual 'e|--4--|--1--|', getline(2)

Given (no-op on non-tab lines):
  this is prose

Execute (no-op on non-tab lines):
  call cursor(1, 1)
  call songwriter#tab#TabChord('Am')
Expect:
  this is prose

Given songwriter (a tab with an annotation line):
      Am
  e|--0--3--|

Execute (6 the chord goes on the annotation line right above the strings when it fits):
  call cursor(2, 8)
  SongwriterTabChord C
  AssertEqual [2, 8], [line('.'), col('.')]

Expect songwriter:
      Am C
  e|--0--3--|

Given songwriter (a tab with an annotation line):
      Am
  e|--0--3--|

Execute (6 the chord needs a space on each side: the tab is widened before it):
  call cursor(2, 7)
  SongwriterTabChord C
  AssertEqual [2, 8], [line('.'), col('.')]

Expect songwriter:
      Am C
  e|--0---3--|

Given songwriter (a tab with labels):
      Am G
  e|--0--3--|

Execute (6 the chord needs a space on each side: the tab is widened after it):
  call cursor(2, 5)
  SongwriterTabChord Cmaj7
  AssertEqual [2, 5], [line('.'), col('.')]

Expect songwriter:
      Cmaj7 G
  e|--0-----3--|

Given songwriter (a tab with a span):
      PM------
  e|--0--3--|

Execute (6 the chord goes on a new line when a span is in the way):
  call cursor(2, 8)
  SongwriterTabChord C
  AssertEqual [3, 8], [line('.'), col('.')]

Expect songwriter:
      PM------
         C
  e|--0--3--|

Given (the chord is spelled canonically, other words as given):
  e|--4--|--1--|
  B|-----|-----|
  G|-----|-----|
  D|-----|-----|
  A|-----|-----|
  E|-----|-----|

Execute (the chord is spelled canonically, other words as given):
  for [typed, spelled] in [['CM7', 'Cmaj7'], ['Amin7', 'Am7'], ['Dsus', 'Dsus4'], ['GM', 'G'],
        \ ['Cadd9', 'Cadd9'], ['Bdim/F', 'Bdim/F'], ['AM7/E', 'Amaj7/E']]
    %delete _
    call setline(1, ['e|--4--|--1--|'] + map(['B', 'G', 'D', 'A', 'E'], 'v:val . "|-----|-----|"'))
    call cursor(1, 5)
    call songwriter#tab#TabChord(typed)
    AssertEqual '    ' . spelled, getline(1), typed
  endfor
